  "question": {
    "text": "In photoelectric effect an em-wave is incident on a metal surface and electrons are ejected from the surface. If the work function of the metal is 2.14 eV and stopping potential is 2 V , what is the wavelength of the em-wave ?\n(Given hc $=1242 \\mathrm{eVnm}$ where h is the Planck's constant and c is the speed of light in vaccum.)"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "300 nm",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "400 nm",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "600 nm",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "200 nm",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\phi=2.14 \\\\\n& V_S=2 \\mathrm{~V}\n\\end{aligned}$\nUsing photoelectric equation.\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{h c}{\\lambda}=2.14+2=4.14 \\mathrm{eV} \\\\\n& \\lambda=\\frac{1242}{4.14}=300 \\mathrm{~nm}\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}